Kimi K3.1 Pro on a DGX Station (2-bit experts under stock vLLM)
===============================================================

This recipe is part of dgx-station-recipes (MIT; see ../LICENSE). Copyright 2026 Tomas Cupr.

Its three-tier layout (hot experts on the GB300, a second tier computed on the RTX PRO 6000 by a sidecar, placement
from measured route counts) and the recipe's shape (CLI, README, RESULTS, LIMITATIONS, NOTICE) follow Garner
McCloud's ../deepseek-v4.1-flash by way of ../glm-5.3-flash-fp8. serve/hook/kchannel.py is glm-5.3-flash-fp8's
peer/channel.py with Kimi's sizes.

The model
---------

moonshotai/Kimi-K3.1-Pro, https://huggingface.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K3.1-Pro, revision
d9e99b0792a5e93b78ea9bea62a68167e36ddd9e. "Kimi K3.1-Pro License", Copyright (c) 2026 Moonshot AI: an MIT-style
licence with additional conditions for Model-as-a-Service businesses above 20 million US dollars of revenue in 12
months (a separate agreement with Moonshot AI) and for products above 100 million monthly active users or 20 million
US dollars of monthly revenue ("Kimi K3.1-Pro" must be displayed). Read the full text in the model repository
(LICENSE) before any commercial use. This repository contains no weights. `kimi install` downloads the
served files, a derivative of that release (routed experts re-rounded to 2 bits, the other weights unchanged),
from huggingface.co/tomcupr/Kimi-K3.1-Pro-DGX-Station-2bit, which carries Moonshot AI's licence and copyright
notice; `kimi prepare` derives the same files from the official release on your machine. serve/rank-native.json is
a table of expert ids ordered by measured use, not weights.

The draft model is Inferact/Kimi-K3.1-Pro-DSpark-preview, under its own licence in its repository.

Code this recipe runs but does not include
------------------------------------------

vLLM (image vllm/vllm-openai:kimi-k31), Apache-2.0: the server, including the Kimi K3 model code the hook attaches
to. The hook calls vLLM's functions; it copies none of its source. PyTorch, Triton, safetensors, transformers: their
own licences. tools/kstream.py and study/ only: Moonshot AI's Kimi K3 reference modeling code (fetched by the user) and fla-core, MIT.

Method
------

study/kgptq.py follows GPTQ (Frantar et al., 2022). The served experts do not use it: plain rounding scored the
same end to end (RESULTS.md).
